---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { SITE, url } from '../config/site';

const { legal, email, analyticsId, fullName } = SITE;
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="How Sam Labenne handles personal information on this website and when you get in touch."
  intro="This site collects as little as possible. There are no forms, no tracking by default, and your details are never sold."
>
  <h2>Who I am</h2>
  <p>
    This website belongs to {fullName} (“I”, “me”), an independent digital builder offering website,
    webshop, Odoo and Salesforce services. I am responsible for (the “controller” of) the personal
    information described here.
  </p>
  {
    (legal.registration || legal.address) && (
      <p>
        {legal.registration && <>{legal.registration}. </>}
        {legal.address && <>Business address: {legal.address}.</>}
      </p>
    )
  }
  <p>
    Questions about privacy can go to <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    This policy is written to meet the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and the
    Australian Privacy Principles in the <em>Privacy Act 1988</em> (Cth).
  </p>

  <h2>What I collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>What you send me.</strong> This site has no forms. If you email me, I receive your
      email address, your name and anything you choose to include in your message.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Technical information.</strong> When you visit, the hosting and network providers
      automatically process technical data such as your IP address, browser type and the pages
      requested, so the site can be delivered and kept secure. I don’t use this to identify you.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Cookies and similar technologies.</strong> Analytics cookies are only used if you
      accept them. See the <a href={url('/cookies/')}>cookie policy</a> for details.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How I use it, and why</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Purpose</th><th>Legal basis (GDPR)</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Replying to your email and discussing a possible project</td>
        <td>Steps you’ve asked me to take before a possible contract, and my legitimate interest in answering enquiries</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Running and securing the website</td>
        <td>My legitimate interest in operating a secure, working website</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Understanding how the website is used (analytics)</td>
        <td>Your consent, which you can withdraw at any time</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Keeping records I’m required to keep</td>
        <td>Legal obligation</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    I don’t sell personal information, I don’t use it for automated decision-making, and I won’t add
    you to a mailing list.
  </p>

  <h2>Who I share it with</h2>
  <p>Personal information is only shared with the services that make this site and my work possible:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>the website host, GitHub (GitHub Pages), and the domain and network provider, Cloudflare;</li>
    <li>my email provider;</li>
    {analyticsId && <li>Google, for website analytics, only if you accept analytics cookies;</li>}
    <li>professional advisers, such as an accountant, where needed.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    These providers may only use the information to provide their services. I may also disclose
    information where the law requires it.
  </p>

  <h2>International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    My business is registered in Australia, I work with clients in Europe and elsewhere, and some of
    these providers are based in other countries, including the United States. When personal information from the
    European Economic Area is transferred abroad, it is protected by recognised safeguards such as
    adequacy decisions (including the EU–US Data Privacy Framework, where a provider is certified)
    or the European Commission’s Standard Contractual Clauses. For Australian personal
    information, I take reasonable steps to make sure overseas recipients handle it consistently
    with the Australian Privacy Principles.
  </p>

  <h2>How long I keep it</h2>
  <p>
    I keep emails only as long as they’re useful to answer and follow up on your enquiry. If we work
    together, I keep project correspondence and records for the length of the project and
    afterwards as long as the law requires (for example, for tax and accounting). Otherwise I delete
    them once they’re no longer needed.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>If you’re in the EU or EEA, you have the right under the GDPR to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>access the personal information I hold about you;</li>
    <li>have it corrected if it’s inaccurate, or deleted;</li>
    <li>restrict or object to how I use it;</li>
    <li>receive it in a portable format;</li>
    <li>withdraw your consent at any time, where I rely on consent; and</li>
    <li>complain to your local data protection authority.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    If you’re in Australia, you can ask to access or correct the personal information I hold about
    you. If you’re unhappy with how I’ve handled it, please contact me first; you can also complain
    to the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner
    (<a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au" rel="noopener">oaic.gov.au</a>).
  </p>
  <p>
    Elsewhere, you may have similar rights under your local law. To make a request, email
    <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>. I’ll reply within one month (or 30 days under
    Australian law) and may need to confirm your identity first.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    The website is served over an encrypted (HTTPS) connection and I take reasonable measures to
    protect the information I hold. No system is completely secure, so please don’t email highly
    sensitive information unless we’ve agreed a secure way to share it.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
  <p>
    This site links to other websites, such as Ksara Events. Their privacy practices are their own,
    so please read their policies.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    I’ll update this policy when anything changes. The date at the top shows when it was last
    revised.
  </p>
</Legal>
